              ISO Technical Committee 156 – Corrosion of Metals and Alloys
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- CONCLUSION & SUMMARY -->
      <section class="section" id="summary" style="margin-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 30px;">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>This section expands the corrosion model by focusing on formulation-driven mechanisms. Both liquid-phase and vapor-phase pathways influence corrosion behavior, while coating performance, solvent interactions, pH drift, humidity cycles, and propellant dynamics determine long-term stability. Understanding these mechanisms enables more accurate prediction of failure modes and supports the engineering of robust water-based aerosol products.</p>
      </section>

